Vikram and Betal: The Honest Farmer’s Son (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100138

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a farmer and his son,” said Betal. “The farmer always taught his son to be honest.”

One day, while working in the field, the boy found a small bag of coins.

He picked it up and ran to his father.

The father said, “We must find the owner and return it.”

They went around the village asking if anyone had lost the bag.

Finally, an old man came forward and said, “I lost my coins!”

The boy returned the bag without taking anything.

The old man was very happy and blessed the boy.

Later, the king heard about the boy’s honesty.

He called him and rewarded him.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, what made the boy special?”

Vikram replied, “He followed the right values and chose honesty.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Honesty and good values lead to respect.
